"""Model card returned by the agent's model_info tool (generated from the benchmark results)."""

CARD = '# GeoAI-GWFM-KR v1.0\n\nGroundwater-level forecasting for Korean monitoring wells. A LoRA adapter for Amazon Chronos-2, trained by\nGeoAI Alignment, Inc. on wells of the National Groundwater Monitoring Network of the Republic of Korea.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Base model | [amazon/chronos-2](https://huggingface.co/amazon/chronos-2) (Apache-2.0), not included; downloaded from Amazon |\n| This package | LoRA adapter, rank 8, 1.2 million parameters (4.9 MB), CC BY-NC 4.0 |\n| Inputs | Daily groundwater level (m) up to the forecast start; daily rainfall (mm), past and for the forecast days |\n| Outputs | Daily level forecasts with the 10%, 50% and 90% quantiles, 1 to 90 days ahead (tested at 7, 30 and 90 days) |\n| Training data | 188 wells at 123 stations, almost all in the Yeongnam region, records up to 2021 |\n| Test data | 46 wells at 30 other stations, held out before training, forecasts for 2023-2024 |\n| Developer | GeoAI Alignment, Inc., Daegu, Republic of Korea, https://geoaialign.ai |\n\n## Tested accuracy\n\nSkill = 1 - RMSE / RMSE of persistence (the last observed level held constant), over all days from day 1 to the horizon. Median over the 46 test\nwells, forecasts every 7 days in 2023-2024, rainfall of the forecast days given as a perfect rainfall forecast.\nAll models received the same input variables (past levels, past and forecast-day rainfall), trained on\ndata up to 2021, chose their settings on 2022, and are averaged over three training seeds.\n\n| Forecaster | 7 days | 30 days | 90 days |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| GeoAI-GWFM-KR | 0.41 | 0.48 | 0.52 |\n| Chronos-2 without the adapter (zero-shot, no training on these data) | 0.21 | 0.26 | 0.31 |\n| Per-well LSTM, trained on each test well\'s own record | 0.37 | 0.30 | 0.33 |\n| Per-well GRU, trained on each test well\'s own record | 0.41 | 0.33 | 0.37 |\n| Per-well LSTM with a groundwater fluctuation-equation loss | 0.39 | 0.29 | 0.34 |\n| Regional LSTM, trained on the same wells as the adapter | 0.25 | 0.20 | 0.24 |\n\n- GeoAI-GWFM-KR was more accurate than the per-well LSTM at 34, 39 and 40 of 46 wells and than the per-well GRU at 32, 38 and 35 at 7, 30 and 90 days,\n  and than Chronos-2 alone at 44-46 wells.\n- Chronos-2 alone showed no significant paired difference from the per-well LSTM at 30 and 90 days\n  (p = 0.084 and p = 0.49) and was less accurate at 7 days.\n- From past rainfall alone, without a rainfall forecast, the gain is smaller (30-day skill 0.16, Chronos-2 alone 0.11).\n- The 80% interval covered 80% of observations at 7 days and 74% at 90 days (70% without a rainfall forecast).\n\n## Intended use\n\nShort- to medium-range forecasts (days to three months) of daily groundwater levels at monitoring wells,\nincluding wells with short records, for water-resource planning, drought watch, monitoring-network\noperation, research and teaching. Rainfall scenarios can be compared by supplying different future rainfall.\n\n## Limits\n\n- Trained and tested in the Yeongnam region. Accuracy in other regions and climates is not yet tested.\n- Tested accuracy assumes a perfect rainfall forecast. Operational rainfall forecasts add their own error.\n- Pumping and other human operations are not inputs; at strongly pumped wells their effect stays in the error.\n- The model forecasts levels; it does not estimate aquifer properties or replace a groundwater flow model.\n\n## Use\n\n```python\nfrom chronos import Chronos2Pipeline\nfrom peft import PeftModel\n\nbase = Chronos2Pipeline.from_pretrained("amazon/chronos-2")\npipe = Chronos2Pipeline(model=PeftModel.from_pretrained(base.model, "GeoAI-GWFM-KR-v1.0").merge_and_unload())\n```\n\nSee `example_inference.py`, or install the `geoai-gwfm` package for the command-line tool and the forecasting agent.\n\n## License and citation\n\nAdapter weights, benchmark split and results, technical notes: CC BY-NC 4.0 (attribution required, noncommercial). Code, including the example: PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0.\nChronos-2 remains under the Apache License 2.0. For commercial licensing contact GeoAI Alignment.\n\nPark, E., Park, J., & Kim, T. (2026). GeoAI-GWFM-KR v1.0: groundwater-level forecasting for Korean monitoring wells, adapted from Chronos-2. GeoAI Alignment, Inc. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23584923\n\nData: National Groundwater Information Center (www.gims.go.kr); Korea Meteorological Administration (data.kma.go.kr).\nChronos-2: Ansari et al. (2025), arXiv:2510.15821.\n'
